codex
The paper’s native object is indeed an undirected simple graph, but its core task is not “find a hidden clique”: Sections 3.1–3.2 define an exact fitness equal to the number of forbidden cliques plus forbidden independent sets, and Section 3.4 searches one-edge neighbors heuristically. The only theorem (Section 2.1) is a degree bound; the paper gives no distributional hardness theorem. I’m therefore testing whether an honest Track B family can use the paper’s one-edge-neighborhood problem without reducing away the graph structure.
