The full text narrows the usable mathematics considerably. The paper has one exact structural theorem (the degree interval), one fixed 35-vertex 8-regular Ramsey core, and four explicit 40-vertex near-solutions; its ABC method is heuristic and supplies no hardness theorem. I’m checking whether Section 3’s exact independent-set counting shortcut can support an honest Track B family before deciding whether this paper must be rejected.
