It is obviously that r(3,10)−graph contains two limitations, that is, neither  
complete graphs of order 3 nor independent sets of order 10. To calculate the Ramsey 
number R(3,10), Jan Goedgebeur and Stanislaw P .Radziszowski  got new 
Computational Upper Bounds for Ramsey Numbers R(3,k) in 2013[2].They have 
proved that 40 ≤ R(3,10) ≤ 42 and anticipated that any further improvement to either 
of the bounds will be very difficult[2]. Despite many attempts  by Exoo , them, and 
others, nor  r(3,10,40)−graphs were constructed[28, 29, 30, 31, 32]. 

