5. The Conclusion 
In this article, visa Artificial Bee Colony to calculate the Ramsey Number R(3,10), 
we achieved four r(3,9,39) graphs at the first time to approximate inf R(3,10). 
We also try to adjust some of the edges in one of these four graphs and always get 
another one of these four graphs or some graphs containing many  10-independent 
sets. So we strongly suspect that these four graphs maybe the best and r(3,10) = 40. 
We can see from the graphs that if we delete vertex 3 or 38 in graph-3 or delete vertex 
37 or vertex 38 in graph -1 then we can get four r(3,9,39) graphs. They may be 
isomorphic to the one already found and maybe not. From these for the first time, four 
graphs we also try to add one more 


=== PAGE 14 ===
