Rejected at Step 0 after reading the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.01613).

The paper provides only fixed near-Ramsey graphs and an uncertified ABC heuristic. A partial-completion family is generatable and verifiable, but:

- Track A has no applicable distributional-hardness theorem.
- Track B has no compression gap: hidden completions require the full search; exposed constructions take the same 24 lookup operations mechanically and compactly.

The complete evidence, section references, exact graph checks, and cost comparisons are in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1512.01613/REJECTED.md). Per the task’s Step 0 rule, no generator or fabricated gate/oracle reports were created.
